      "what": "A spell, ritual or incantation is cast, learned, studied, attempted or discussed as something the investigator might do.",
      "not_for": "A Mythos book merely carried or opened; a rite seen performed by others.",
      "examples": [
        "我试着念出那页上的咒文",
        "照书上说的画一个圆",
        "我想学这个法术"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "time_passes",
      "trigger": "jev",
      "what": "The declared action spends real time or draws attention: waiting, resting, sleeping, a long search or job, travel, working through records, making noise, lighting a fire, being seen or heard.",
      "not_for": "A quick exchange of words; a glance; a single immediate act.",
      "examples": [
        "我在旅馆睡一晚",
        "把整个档案室翻一遍",
        "在棚下等到天黑",
        "开车去下一个镇"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "_notes_20261004": "After the first full replay (59 turns): st/clues gains the clue_search topic (the section also carries 'where next'); ei/manage drops carried_item (14 false loads, 2 needed); kp/clocks becomes topic time_passes gated on a running clock (21 loads, 1 needed when state-only); the first-impression gate reads last_spoke_turn (met_turns already counts the opening scene). After the third replay: the stall and recover sections load only when their counter is up AND the words involve no topic (the stuck case: a stalled counter with nothing to do), halving the loads at equal recall; the register section asks carried_item at 0.7."
